senses.gloss:
vibuddha, ppp. (not noted in Pali; Skt. id., in somewhat different mgs.),
(1) thoroughly enlightened: sātivibuddha (= sa ati-vi˚, O thou who art exceedingly well enlightened!) pravartaya cakravaraṃ LV 〔415.4〕 (vs);
(2) made noticeable, conspicuous: prāsāda-harmiyaṃ taṃ (mss. ˚harmiye) gavākṣa-vara-śaraṇa-pañjara-vibuddhaṃ Mv 〔ii.36.4〕 (vs).
